WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.720
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.050
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.260
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:19.790
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:30.040
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.470
Go! Go!

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.850
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.750
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.120
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:50.120
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.500
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.940
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.070
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.550
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.910
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.280
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.680
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:20.590
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.070
May, get the regulator for terminal three.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:35.720
Right!

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:37.560
May, some solder.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.220
Right!

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.540
Layered ceramic condenser.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.230
Right!

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.530
More solder and pine tar.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.270
Right!

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.580
Wipe, wipe, wipe, wipe...

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:54.590
Okay, then...

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.420
Ikariya! Version upgrade!

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.020
Kazuya, how is he any different?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.640
Yo!

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.690
Uh, yo...

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.440
Too soft! Yo!

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.530
Yo!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.740
Again!

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.820
Yo!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.780
Let's give today everything we've got!

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.950
Oh, Kazuya, it's wonderful! Isn't it wonderful, Ikariya?!

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:31.400
Wonderful, wonderful! Wonderful, wonderful! Wonderful, wonderful!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.700
Thanks, but he's nowhere near as good as you, May.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.180
<i>Yeah, he's not as good as May yet...</i>

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.170
<i>If only Ikariya could move by his own will, like May does.</i>

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.660
<i>I'd like to study May for that. And if I do, then...</i>

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.140
Kazuya! Please don't do this!

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.250
Kazuya, please don't...

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.500
Come on, May! Show me everything you're made of!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.850
If I know everything, then I... I...!

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.500
NO!

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:12.830
Kazuya?

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.000
What's wrong?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.840
Uh, I wasn't thinking about taking you apart at all!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.760
Oh?

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.890
That's right. This is a problem I'll just have to solve myself, yeah.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.390
Right!

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.260
I'll give it everything I've got!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.230
Damn it all! Damn it all!

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.690
DAMN IT ALL!

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.230
And by that, I don't mean to say...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.230
Starch and ancient crypts, what time is it?!

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.070
6:35 in the morning. No, forget that!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.160
It's what you say when everything goes wrong!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.410
So what else is new?

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:48.160
What I want to hear is Kazuya Saotome

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:53.820
screaming "Damn it all!" when we steal that mini-bot May!

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.550
Now, if you understand that, hurry up and eat your ramen and recover that mini-bot.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.130
That's your job, right?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.260
And why should I obey someone who's not my superior?

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.470
Oh, I see...

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.310
And here I had this yummy miso butter corn ramen

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.350
specially sent here from Hokkaido. Oh, well.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.420
Guess I'll have to throw it out.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.610
Your wish is my command, Master Nanbara!

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.530
Then be on your way!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.100
Oh, never fear, sir. I already...

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.040
have a plan.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.320
My superiors at the Cyberdyne Corporation

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.570
have given me a manual for how to reclaim the cyber doll!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:38.380
After comparing the data on Kazuya Saotome that
you gave me to the manual, the result became clear!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.670
Result?!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.890
Kazuya Saotome is gutless around women,

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.720
and there's one specific type he just can't resist!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.260
I believe we should use a cyber doll of that type to recover...

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.260
I see, I see. So, what type is it?

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.680
Oh, for Pete's sake...

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.810
The data's on this.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.330
The disc!

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.200
May...

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.050
Yes?

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:12.120
Okay, if it looks like anyone sees you, pretend you're a doll.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.810
Right.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.520
What's the point in seeing the recovery cyber doll?

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.210
Let's go back for that ramen.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.340
Don't be stupid, Sara.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.550
If we watch what happens, I get to see Saotome's face go...!

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.430
You see? Two birds with one stone.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.920
And rolling stones gather no...

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.390
Okay, out of 5000 yen...

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.640
And that's 469 yen for your change.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.610
There. Better double-check that.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.320
Uh... S-Sure...

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.170
Is that her?!

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.660
I-It's all here.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.860
Thank you, and please come again!

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:54.870
May I help you?

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.620
Nothing happened!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:57.670
Yeah...

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.960
Okay, now I have all the stuff I need for Ikariya.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.920
So, you're going to upgrade Ikariya again, soon?

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.340
Yeah. I hope it gets us even one day closer

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.370
to having him be like you, May.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.180
Ow...

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.190
May?! May?!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.690
Are you okay?

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.950
You aren't hurt, are you?

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.820
Uh, yeah! I mean, no! I'm fine.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.350
You dropped this.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:33.410
<i>I'm a doll. I'm a doll.</i>

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.080
Th-Thanks a lot.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.950
It's a cute doll.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.370
I'd like a doll like this one!

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.090
That high school girl?

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.550
The recovery unit.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:48.510
Here you go.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.970
Don't drop her again, okay? See you.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.470
She's just a normal high school girl!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.770
Seems that way.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.230
Um, Kazuya?

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.520
Fallen for her?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.610
Love at first sight, huh?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.030
N-No way!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:08.610
I was just thinking what a thoughtful girl she was!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:12.950
Boy, guys are always to so quick to be evasive.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.910
That's... not true. I'm not being evasive.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.790
Really?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:21.420
Then show me how that doll talks and moves.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.880
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.130
You see? You're being evasive again!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.880
Well, I saw it all.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.260
You were walking with that doll in your pocket and talking to her.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.180
Hello. I'm May the doll!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.890
What's your name?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.140
It's Rena.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:43.020
Rena, I'm a doll, so I can't talk or move. Understand?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.320
Why's he playing with that kid?!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:51.110
You must have imagined it, right? So... So... Um...

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.320
You're teasing me...

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.070
YOU'RE TEASING ME!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.460
God, she's insanely loud!

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.030
What?! Did you call me insane?!

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.550
I'm Ikariya! Yo!

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:23.140
He said he's named Ikariya! I'm Rena! How do you do?

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.060
We're saved...

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.230
Thanks to Ikariya.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:31.860
Hey! I told you it talks!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.160
The secret's out.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.320
Yeah...

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.870
Rena, May's a secret, understand?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.790
Uh-huh. I understand, uh...

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.380
It's Kazuya.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.710
Okay, Kazuya! It's a secret!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.260
Wow, so this is coffee, huh?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.710
I've always wanted to try it.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.180
Bleaugh...

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.750
Oh, here. Try putting some sugar in it.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:05.980
It won't be so bitter then.

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:09.110
Rena, where are your mom and dad?

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.400
Weren't you with them?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.400
Well, today's the first day I was allowed to go out alone.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.400
I've never been in this city before.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:16.410
Is your home close by?
I've never been in this city before.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.120
Is your home close by?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.580
Uh-uh, it's really far away.

00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:23.200
You think she's lost?

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.160
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.630
Mmm! It's good!

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:34.760
Oh, I'm bored! Nothing's happening at all!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.550
And there's no ramen here, either...

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.470
Oh, I'm sorry, May!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.520
Let's go clean you off in the bathroom.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.980
It's all right. I'll just wipe it off with this.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.940
That's no good. Let's go, May!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.860
Anything wrong?

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.730
Oh, excuse me. We had a little spill here.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.280
Are you all right? Hm?

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:56.860
Oh, dear.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.240
I'll get her cleaned up right away.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.700
Th- Thank you.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.990
<i>I'm a doll. I'm a doll.</i>

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:09.500
It's a very cute doll. I want to take her home with me.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.930
There you go.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.510
Thank you very much.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.210
Enjoy your drinks.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.060
I said I wanted to do it for you.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.390
Yes, you did, but...

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.850
If you don't get home soon,

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:31.110
your mom and dad are going to get worried.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:34.730
That's okay. I may not look it, but I can take care of myself.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.030
I even have a job to do.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.210
You're a smart girl, Rena!

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:39.960
Well...

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:46.160
Ma'am?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.540
Let me carry that for you.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.180
Oh, thank you so much.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:50.720
Come on, let's cross.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.420
You don't suppose the old lady's the recovery unit, do you?

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.840
Damn that Saotome! His safety zone just keeps expanding!

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.930
The signal!

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.310
It's no use, May.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.150
Ma'am, get on my back.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.710
Sorry for the trouble.

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:26.870
Kazuya, hurry up!

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.870
Huh? Right!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.340
Bye, Granny! Take care!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.470
Bye-bye!

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.130
Okay, let's go, Kazuya.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.940
You okay, Rena?

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.110
Y-Yeah, I'm okay.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:00.280
Kazuya's a lot stronger than he looks.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.610
He can lift a whole liter of milk with one hand!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:06.200
Uh, May, that's really not that impressive.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.080
Huh? <i>I</i> thought it was really impressive!

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.330
Kazuya, you're so nice...

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:12.540
I thought.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.000
Her name is Rena, and she's lost, huh?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.040
Yes, sir. Take care of her, please.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.210
Well, take care, Rena.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.010
See you next week!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.340
Sorry for the bother.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.840
No problem. Thank you.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.930
I didn't do anything wrong. Why'd he leave me here?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.060
That should do it. Okay, here goes!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.360
Ikariya, massively upgraded!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:42.070
You did it, Kazuya! Okay, the milk's poured now.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:49.740
Kazuya, do you think Rena got home all right?

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.710
Yeah. She's fine.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.670
Right! Coming!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.700
Who's there... Huh?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.170
Is this the home of Mr. Kazuya Saotome?

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.090
Yes.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.510
You're sure, now?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.590
I'm home!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.350
Rena?!

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:12.560
When we asked about her guardians, we were told they were here.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:16.520
Neglecting a child is a terrible thing to do!

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:20.540
I'm going to take you to the station and teach you a lesson.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.650
Come on, let's go.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.150
Wait! This is a mistake!

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.150
Come on!

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:28.950
Bye-bye! See you later!

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:30.780
Kazuya...

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.920
Serves you right! Sara, that has to be the recovery unit!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.210
Nope.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:44.620
The recovery unit would have taken Cyber Doll May only.

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.070
Who cares, as long as it causes Kazuya Saotome misfortune!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:53.800
Cyber Doll May!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.520
What?

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.770
Rena, where are we going?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.940
That way.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:01.980
But I was told no one else was supposed to see me.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.400
So let's wait for Kazuya and go there together.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.740
Can't. We have to go now.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.820
Rena, please...

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.910
But I have to go <i>now!</i>

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:17.580
Um, o-okay, as long as it doesn't take too long.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.210
Really?!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.760
S-Sure. But we have to go back as soon as we can, okay?

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.530
<i>Kazuya, what should I do?</i>

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:33.390
Getting a phone call from the cops like that...

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.640
I was really surprised!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:39.440
Sorry, Kasumi. I didn't know who else to call.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.690
No prob, no prob.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:44.400
Still, you found a real little trouble-maker, didn't you?

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:48.270
I figure she got lost and felt lonely, and, well...

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:49.860
besides that—

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.710
Hello?! Shikishima?!

00:14:56.710 --> 00:15:00.370
Please give me the rent! Shikishima!

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.920
May... Rena!

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.980
Shikishima? I know you're in there!

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:18.890
Clumsy, isn't she?

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.110
That's the 13th time she's done that.

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:23.310
Rena, are you all right?

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.480
No problem!

00:15:26.770 --> 00:15:28.990
I can't keep waiting for the recovery like this!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.410
I'll take the mini-bot back with my own hands!

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.870
Sara, you want to eat that ramen soon, don't you?!

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:34.870
I'm in!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:37.540
Let's go back, Rena.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.660
Hold it right there, mini-bot! And you, brat!

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:45.620
Now hand the mini-bot over to
Mr. Nanbara like a good little brat!

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.090
There's no place to run!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.130
I remember you!

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:54.220
Come on! Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:55.840
COME ON!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.360
That was...

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:10.030
They must be bad guys if they want to catch you, May!

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.100
Okay!

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:17.870
Where'd that brat run off to?!

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:21.790
Hey, I'm over here! HEY!

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.070
Why, that...!

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:26.130
Don't move from there, brat!

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:29.550
Rena?

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:37.050
This is fun! Let's do some more!

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:54.360
More! More!

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:58.490
Kazuya.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.530
Rena, stop it now.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:02.540
What do you mean? I don't understand!
Rena, stop it now.

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.830
What do you mean? I don't understand!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:09.250
You're a cyber doll, too, aren't you?

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:13.260
So, that's why she could do that stuff.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.760
Yeah. You figured it out.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:19.550
You were protecting May. Thank you.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.140
Well, it wasn't anything that great.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:24.180
But she <i>was</i> great, you know?

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.560
The way she just snapped her fingers

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.010
and made the light change—

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:32.190
It's not like that, Kazuya!

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:40.780
It's not like that! Rena did it to save me!

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:45.200
I know. But take a good look around us.

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:00.470
I don't know how to put this,

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:04.270
but I just don't think it's right to upset other people.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:08.250
I think that goes for humans and for cyber dolls.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.760
I-I don't...

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.070
Rena...

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.720
I don't...

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:20.780
I don't understand! Kazuya, I hate you!

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.430
Rena!

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:25.290
It's my fault.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:30.310
If I'd just kept her in the apartment until you came back...

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.670
So, Kazuya, please...

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.260
Why does this happen to us?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.140
Ra-a-a-a-men...

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.000
Stupid...

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.230
Stupid Kazuya...

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.580
HELP ME!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.750
Come back here, you...!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.210
Ikariya?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.820
You can't escape!

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.220
What's the big idea, Ikariya?!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:26.180
What's the problem?! I'm just playing Catch May!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:31.840
Well, I'm not her, so why'd you spray ink all over me?!

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:37.580
Why? Why would you make me feel bad?

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:42.780
Look, Ikariya...

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:43.780
What?!

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:49.250
Playing's okay, but you shouldn't cause trouble for other people.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.880
You're a good boy. You understand, right?

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:56.170
Yeah, I understand.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:59.010
Oh, Ikariya!

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.930
Rena's a robot, like May is?!

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:13.440
We're called cyber dolls.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:18.960
I'm not sure of the details, but she says that she doesn't want to go back,

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.490
so I was wondering...

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.070
Stop!

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:25.200
Rena, come over to my house.

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:29.600
If you stay at my place, you can come here to play with Ikariya whenever you want to.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.170
You've already got May over here.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.280
How would it look if you had a little girl here, too?

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:36.290
I hear you!
How would it look if you had a little girl here, too?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.670
I hear you!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:39.740
How it would look?

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.380
<i>Hi-ho! Rena here!</i>

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.970
<i>I was asked to reclaim Cyber Doll May,</i>

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.640
<i>but since she's Ikariya's friend, I won't do it.</i>

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.310
<i>I'll be staying here for a while, so see you later!</i>

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.980
Sara! What's this?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.900
What do you think? It's V-mail from the recovery unit.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.970
That brat is the recovery unit?!

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:02.690
Hey, I didn't know, either!

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.640
WHAT DO YOU MEAN YOU DIDN'T KNOW?!

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:12.160
<i>Rena's younger than me, but a lot bigger than me, too.</i>

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.160
<i>She's amazingly loud when she cries,</i>

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.980
<i>but she's really a very sweet little girl.</i>

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:19.290
<i>Kazuya could see that without any trouble.</i>

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:23.190
<i>It'll be even more fun having another friend around here.</i>

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.680
<i>I don't want to lose to someone as full of energy as Rena is,</i>

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:28.560
<i>so tomorrow, like always, I'm going to give this job my best!</i>

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:46.010
When I'm with you, I blush till my ears turn red.

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:50.210
I wonder why that is...

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:56.450
When I'm alone with you I can never seem to do anything right.

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:03.620
I become so tongue-tied I can't speak at all.

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:11.430
It's strange, don't you think? I think about it too much.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:20.570
Is this love? I just can't accept that at all.

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:27.580
I can't be honest. I want so much to be.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:34.260
Someday, perhaps, you'll tell me

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:41.860
the true feelings that are in my heart.

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:45.420
Hey, Sara!

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:45.920
Yeah?

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:49.220
We have to practice how we'll laugh when we get Saotome! Ready?!

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:49.790
Eh?

00:22:51.860 --> 00:22:52.370
Again!

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:56.930
What a face you've got!

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:58.470
"Please Don't Look!"
